# The box: Corner radius rounds the background, the border and the clipping of an image, and of what reaches the corner inside.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: The box · Rounded corners
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: row
			Gap: 20
			Vertical: top
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 20 0
	Section:
		Text: The box
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Rounded corners
		Paragraph: `Corner radius` rounds the corners: one value for all four, or one per corner. It only changes how the box is painted. A child that reaches a rounded corner is clipped by it, without rounding the child, and an image is clipped by the corners of its own box.
			Style: intro
		Stack:
			Style: row
			Item:
				Block:
					Text: Corner radius: 8
						Style: label
